WEBVTT

00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:15.170
<i>At the personal request of President Hyoudou,</i>

00:00:15.170 --> 00:00:19.490
<i>Tonegawa has been tasked with 
devising a diabolical death game.</i>

00:00:20.490 --> 00:00:25.710
<i>Repeated failures cause him to 
nearly lose the faith of his men!</i>

00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:29.660
<i>So he stakes it all on a 
gamble to redeem himself.</i>

00:00:29.660 --> 00:00:33.230
<i>To overcome the gap separating 
him from his men,</i>

00:00:33.230 --> 00:00:36.340
<i>he hosts an employee vacation!</i>

00:00:36.770 --> 00:00:41.600
<i>And it's a huge success!</i>

00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:48.600
<i>Their trust: regained! Tonegawa: revived!</i>

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:50.840
<i>He rises like a phoenix!</i>

00:00:53.140 --> 00:00:57.870
<i>He has once again climbed to the 
heady heights of being the boss!</i>

00:01:12.680 --> 00:01:14.030
<i>"Overtime."</i>

00:01:14.030 --> 00:01:17.880
<i>A disgraceful display put on by people 
who don't work efficiently enough.</i>

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:21.810
<i>It's not as if they get work done 
just by being in the building.</i>

00:01:21.810 --> 00:01:27.220
<i>But it looks like no one from my team is 
wasting their time with that nonsense.</i>

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:30.690
<i>Of course not. The men on my team are...</i>

00:01:33.290 --> 00:01:36.150
Oh, Tonegawa-sensei. Heading home?

00:01:36.150 --> 00:01:39.450
Yeah. You haven't finished yet?

00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:40.030
<b>Psst...</b>

00:01:40.760 --> 00:01:43.970
Nope, I'm working overtime. 
Have a good night, sir.

00:01:52.370 --> 00:01:54.580
I probably shouldn't expect much

00:01:54.580 --> 00:01:57.550
from him at tomorrow's meeting.

00:01:57.890 --> 00:02:01.800
<i>Tonegawa, once again, heads home on time!</i>

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:04.490
Oh...

00:02:05.220 --> 00:02:06.870
<i>Forgot my phone.</i>

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:15.970
<i>Tonegawa Yukio, the number two 
man of the massive Teiai Group.</i>

00:02:17.290 --> 00:02:19.680
<i>He serves the monster 
of the financial sector.</i>

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:23.990
<i>This shot-caller rose to the position 
of President Hyoudou's right-hand man.</i>

00:02:25.490 --> 00:02:28.780
<i>This is the story of the battles 
he waged as a middle manager,</i>

00:02:28.780 --> 00:02:32.170
<i>in the shadows of the glory 
and fame he achieved...</i>

00:02:32.170 --> 00:02:40.530
<i>The small, unremarkable story... 
about the struggles of a remarkable man.</i>

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:51.150
<b>Middle Management Blues</b>

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:51.150
<b><i>Mr. Tonegawa</i></b>

00:04:12.230 --> 00:04:14.690
Agenda 03
<b>Adult</b>

00:04:18.760 --> 00:04:22.790
<i>Can I really expect anything 
decent from the others?</i>

00:04:23.490 --> 00:04:26.030
<i>An idea that will give us a breakthrough...</i>

00:04:26.390 --> 00:04:30.520
<i>Without one, we'll just be 
spinning our wheels again.</i>

00:04:33.530 --> 00:04:35.080
Drop me off in front of the station.

00:04:42.820 --> 00:04:45.850
<i>I'll have to think of something myself.</i>

00:04:45.850 --> 00:04:50.020
<i>I might find a hint in these huge crowds...</i>

00:04:52.180 --> 00:04:53.180
<b>Precise Touch</b>

00:04:56.480 --> 00:04:57.980
Yamanote Line    Shinagawa

00:05:02.390 --> 00:05:04.360
Hey, get in line.

00:05:04.360 --> 00:05:06.490
Huh? What's your problem, old man?

00:05:06.870 --> 00:05:08.740
What'd you tell the chief?

00:05:08.740 --> 00:05:11.240
Do I really need to check in with him?

00:05:11.710 --> 00:05:13.190
He'd just get in the way.

00:05:13.190 --> 00:05:15.800
What? Are you serious?
That's not what you promised!

00:05:15.800 --> 00:05:17.250
I'm so pissed right now!

00:05:18.130 --> 00:05:20.750
<i>They seem so orderly at a glance...</i>

00:05:20.750 --> 00:05:23.450
<i>But underneath it lies the 
simmering of their true nature</i>

00:05:23.450 --> 00:05:25.190
<i>and their personal affairs.</i>

00:05:25.190 --> 00:05:28.010
<i>An odd sight, if you think about it.</i>

00:05:28.500 --> 00:05:31.260
<i>A train is approaching on track 5.</i>

00:05:31.260 --> 00:05:35.580
<i>For your safety, please remain 
behind the yellow line.</i>

00:05:35.270 --> 00:05:38.260
<i>It's a microcosm of society itself.</i>

00:05:40.560 --> 00:05:41.650
<b>30</b> mins
to Laketown Station

00:05:40.560 --> 00:05:41.650
<b>Kita-senju</b>

00:05:40.560 --> 00:05:41.650
<b>Matsudo</b>

00:05:40.560 --> 00:05:41.650
<b>Shim-Matsudo</b>

00:05:40.560 --> 00:05:41.650
<b>Ueno</b>

00:05:40.560 --> 00:05:41.650
<b>Soka</b>

00:05:40.560 --> 00:05:41.650
<b>Minami-Urawa</b>

00:05:40.560 --> 00:05:41.650
<b>Minami-Koshigaya</b>

00:05:40.560 --> 00:05:41.650
<b>Shin-Koshigaya</b>

00:05:40.560 --> 00:05:41.650
<b>Akabane</b>

00:05:43.140 --> 00:05:45.590
<i>He's struck by inspiration!</i>

00:05:45.590 --> 00:05:48.160
<i>Like a bolt of lightning! 
A fleeting flash of light!</i>

00:05:48.850 --> 00:05:51.030
<i>Something just...</i>

00:05:55.410 --> 00:05:57.410
<b>Heiwa Sushi</b>

00:06:02.410 --> 00:06:05.410
<i>I know I almost had something.</i>

00:06:05.410 --> 00:06:07.020
Did you remember the ponzu sauce?

00:06:07.020 --> 00:06:08.380
Yep. Plenty of ponzu.

00:06:08.800 --> 00:06:09.550
<i>Pon?</i>

00:06:08.950 --> 00:06:09.550
<b>Pon?</b>

00:06:09.980 --> 00:06:12.940
Look, yammering on and on 
isn't gonna get us anywhere!

00:06:12.940 --> 00:06:14.220
We need evidence, moron!

00:06:14.580 --> 00:06:15.180
<i>Ron!</i>

00:06:14.580 --> 00:06:15.180
<b>Ron!!</b>

00:06:15.680 --> 00:06:17.220
Hey, I didn't order this.

00:06:17.220 --> 00:06:18.640
Wanna pass on the freebie, then?

00:06:18.640 --> 00:06:20.440
<i>P-Pass?!</i>

00:06:19.080 --> 00:06:20.440
<b>Pass!!</b>

00:06:22.020 --> 00:06:24.650
Not gonna eat, sir?

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:26.940
Oh... sorry.

00:06:31.950 --> 00:06:33.140
<i>In the darkness...</i>

00:06:33.800 --> 00:06:35.370
<i>It descends.</i>

00:06:35.370 --> 00:06:40.460
<i>Inspiration opens the door to a breakthrough!</i>

00:06:40.460 --> 00:06:41.830
<b>Heiwa Sushi</b>

00:06:41.830 --> 00:06:42.330
<b>Raise a glass
with us!</b>

00:06:41.830 --> 00:06:42.330
<b>Asohi
Hyper
Dry</b>

00:06:48.280 --> 00:06:49.840
Pops, let me get my check.

00:06:50.970 --> 00:06:52.710
Nothing more to drink?

00:06:52.710 --> 00:06:55.000
Yeah. I'm done for now.

00:06:55.000 --> 00:06:56.970
Sure. Bring the man his check!

00:06:57.810 --> 00:07:01.480
<i>I'm going to have to dive in myself.</i>

00:07:03.400 --> 00:07:08.100
<i>Sometimes you need to take 
do-or-die risks to find a way forward.</i>

00:07:22.250 --> 00:07:26.250
Sometimes death
is salvation.

00:07:23.720 --> 00:07:26.250
<i>"Sometimes death is salvation."</i>

00:07:26.250 --> 00:07:28.890
<i>Tonegawa brainstorms!</i>

00:07:28.890 --> 00:07:31.750
<i>A way to personally lift 
himself out of the fire!</i>

00:07:36.120 --> 00:07:38.760
<i>And the next day...</i>

00:07:39.670 --> 00:07:43.230
<i>We return to Meeting Room 3.</i>

00:07:44.260 --> 00:07:46.730
So, today we're going to continue coming up

00:07:46.730 --> 00:07:52.250
with standout ideas to entertain 
president Hyoudou with.

00:07:52.250 --> 00:07:52.990
<i>Psst, psst...</i>

00:07:53.680 --> 00:07:55.990
That's what I thought I'd be saying, but...

00:07:55.990 --> 00:07:57.210
<i>Psst...</i>

00:07:58.410 --> 00:07:59.790
It came to me...

00:07:59.790 --> 00:08:00.590
<i>Psst...</i>

00:08:00.590 --> 00:08:02.290
While I was out last night.

00:08:02.290 --> 00:08:04.670
<i>Psst.... Psst...</i>

00:08:05.050 --> 00:08:06.160
Inspiration.

00:08:06.160 --> 00:08:06.790
<i>Psst...</i>

00:08:07.450 --> 00:08:09.360
A brilliant concept.

00:08:09.360 --> 00:08:10.050
<i>Psst...</i>

00:08:10.490 --> 00:08:11.790
An idea!

00:08:11.790 --> 00:08:14.670
<i>Psst... Psst, psst... Psst...</i>

00:08:14.670 --> 00:08:15.300
Come on in.

00:08:15.300 --> 00:08:16.310
Sir.

00:08:22.520 --> 00:08:26.090
It was made in a rush, so it's a bit cheap.

00:08:26.090 --> 00:08:27.730
Keep that in mind.

00:08:28.100 --> 00:08:32.490
This is the core of the diabolic 
game I've come up with.

00:08:35.170 --> 00:08:36.040
Do it.

00:08:36.040 --> 00:08:37.240
Yes, sir.

00:08:42.020 --> 00:08:42.870
<b>Psst...</b>

00:08:43.480 --> 00:08:44.690
A name tag?

00:08:44.620 --> 00:08:47.630
<b>Psst... Psst...</b>

00:08:48.690 --> 00:08:51.480
Not bringing anything to mind at all?

00:08:51.480 --> 00:08:52.760
It... says "east."

00:08:53.260 --> 00:08:54.510
Is that all?

00:08:57.700 --> 00:08:58.640
<b>Ton</b>

00:08:57.910 --> 00:08:58.640
"Ton."

00:09:00.640 --> 00:09:04.890
To think only one of you would catch on...

00:09:04.890 --> 00:09:06.610
Well, no matter.

00:09:10.820 --> 00:09:14.610
<i>It begins! An overwhelming presentation!</i>

00:09:14.610 --> 00:09:17.110
Human Mahjong
Debtors = Tiles
A battle among a motley crowd of filth

00:09:17.110 --> 00:09:18.720
Human...

00:09:18.720 --> 00:09:19.970
...Mahjong?!

00:09:19.970 --> 00:09:21.370
<b>Psst...</b>

00:09:22.900 --> 00:09:26.280
It'd be played on an unprecedented scale,
with an assembly of debtors

00:09:26.280 --> 00:09:28.000
acting as the tiles!

00:09:28.760 --> 00:09:30.290
Human Mahjong!

00:09:30.290 --> 00:09:31.750
<b>Psst...</b>

00:09:31.750 --> 00:09:34.200
<i>Human... Mahjong.</i>

00:09:31.750 --> 00:09:37.760
<b>Psst... Psst...</b>

00:09:34.680 --> 00:09:37.760
<i>Tonegawa's proposed diabolic game</i>

00:09:38.280 --> 00:09:42.010
<i>is Human Mahjong!</i>

00:09:38.280 --> 00:09:42.010
<b>Human Mahjong</b>

00:09:42.820 --> 00:09:45.660
<i>The rules are the same as ordinary mahjong.</i>

00:09:45.660 --> 00:09:50.220
<i>It begins with four teams consisting 
of thirteen members each.</i>

00:09:50.220 --> 00:09:54.290
<i>In other words, the same number 
as the initial draw in mahjong,</i>

00:09:54.290 --> 00:09:56.280
<i>the first thirteen tiles in your hand.</i>

00:09:56.280 --> 00:10:02.530
<i>The remaining players wait 
in the center, as the wall.</i>

00:10:03.810 --> 00:10:04.790
It starts...

00:10:06.290 --> 00:10:11.080
Each team begins to draw 
human tiles from the wall.

00:10:12.570 --> 00:10:14.420
This is the real crux of the game.

00:10:14.770 --> 00:10:17.550
In order to choose which tiles to discard...

00:10:19.210 --> 00:10:21.050
They debate!

00:10:21.530 --> 00:10:24.070
As for the tiles that are discarded...

00:10:24.070 --> 00:10:27.810
They're the ones who don't 
get any of the winnings.

00:10:28.250 --> 00:10:30.160
Obviously, they'll be desperate.

00:10:28.250 --> 00:10:30.160
We don't need you!

00:10:30.160 --> 00:10:32.540
Screw you! I might be a reverse dora!

00:10:32.540 --> 00:10:36.150
They'll fight tooth and nail 
to avoid being discarded.

00:10:36.150 --> 00:10:37.870
Who asked you, you trash tile?!

00:10:37.870 --> 00:10:39.230
In essence...

00:10:39.230 --> 00:10:42.200
If only you hadn't gotten that pon!

00:10:42.200 --> 00:10:45.970
They'd be teams in name only. 
It'd be dog eat dog!

00:10:45.970 --> 00:10:46.830
However!

00:10:47.210 --> 00:10:50.610
If a faction like this forms within the team...

00:10:50.610 --> 00:10:54.340
These three become inseparable. 
They're united as friends.

00:10:54.340 --> 00:10:57.460
Okay! The three of us are in the same boat!

00:10:57.460 --> 00:10:59.370
None of us can be discarded!

00:10:59.370 --> 00:11:00.100
Right!

00:11:00.100 --> 00:11:03.350
We're friends! The three of us are one!

00:11:04.440 --> 00:11:05.370
But then...

00:11:04.780 --> 00:11:05.970
<b>Psst... Psst...</b>

00:11:06.600 --> 00:11:07.970
What if...

00:11:14.360 --> 00:11:16.330
You guys! We promised, right?!

00:11:16.330 --> 00:11:17.750
No one gets discarded!

00:11:17.750 --> 00:11:19.480
And we're friends, right?!

00:11:19.480 --> 00:11:21.070
Tanyao...

00:11:21.460 --> 00:11:22.760
Tanyao.

00:11:24.130 --> 00:11:25.670
<i>Tanyao!</i>

00:11:25.670 --> 00:11:29.430
<i>A hand that can only be made 
without number tiles 1 and 8!</i>

00:11:29.430 --> 00:11:31.080
We could get a tanyao...

00:11:32.070 --> 00:11:33.330
You guys!

00:11:33.330 --> 00:11:36.630
You're in the way of our 
tanyao, you 1 of circles!

00:11:37.030 --> 00:11:40.980
<i>Human instinct, totally exposed 
by a diabolic game of mahjong!</i>

00:11:40.980 --> 00:11:44.050
<i>Yes! That is Human Mahjong!</i>

00:11:44.660 --> 00:11:48.150
<i>Are the humans playing mahjong? 
Or is the mahjong playing humans?</i>

00:11:48.150 --> 00:11:50.100
<i>A sublime concept!</i>

00:11:50.100 --> 00:11:55.110
Human Mahjong
Debtors = Tiles
A battle among a motley crowd of filth

00:11:52.010 --> 00:11:54.320
Betrayal. Deception.

00:11:54.320 --> 00:11:55.680
Dissent.

00:11:55.680 --> 00:11:58.170
You forsake and are forsaken...

00:11:58.170 --> 00:11:59.860
Doesn't it remind you of anything?

00:12:00.810 --> 00:12:03.880
It's exactly like society itself!

00:12:03.680 --> 00:12:05.370
<b>Psst... Psst...</b>

00:12:06.920 --> 00:12:10.120
I believe the president would love it.

00:12:10.750 --> 00:12:15.880
The sight of the trash bitterly 
feuding among themselves...

00:12:17.670 --> 00:12:20.030
This is it. This is authentic!

00:12:20.030 --> 00:12:22.730
Human nature on display!

00:12:25.350 --> 00:12:29.140
<i>That is true entertainment. True amusement.</i>

00:12:30.290 --> 00:12:32.520
<b>Psst...</b>

00:12:32.520 --> 00:12:34.620
<i>I-Incredible.</i>

00:12:34.620 --> 00:12:38.150
<i>After erasing all the ideas we 
came up with at the last meeting,</i>

00:12:38.150 --> 00:12:40.030
<i>and setting the bar so high...</i>

00:12:44.570 --> 00:12:47.870
<i>He still cleared it! Tonegawa-sensei 
made it over on his own!</i>

00:12:47.870 --> 00:12:50.550
<i>He's proven himself as our boss!</i>

00:12:53.320 --> 00:12:56.710
Do you think we'd be able to get
enough participants, though?

00:12:56.710 --> 00:12:58.840
<i>No! There is one doubter!</i>

00:12:58.350 --> 00:13:00.210
<b>Psst... Psst...</b>

00:13:05.320 --> 00:13:06.530
Double or nothing.

00:13:08.010 --> 00:13:10.970
<b>Psst... Psst...</b>

00:13:10.970 --> 00:13:12.000
Saemon!

00:13:12.000 --> 00:13:12.720
You idiot!

00:13:13.150 --> 00:13:14.980
It's fine. Go on.

00:13:15.620 --> 00:13:17.550
Well, it's just...

00:13:17.550 --> 00:13:21.880
Gathering the 136 debtors we'd need 
for all the mahjong tiles...

00:13:21.880 --> 00:13:25.110
seems unlikely... or, well, impossible.

00:13:25.110 --> 00:13:28.240
<b>Psst... Psst...</b>

00:13:27.660 --> 00:13:32.200
Plus, there are a lot of people who 
don't know how to play mahjong.

00:13:32.660 --> 00:13:34.160
It wouldn't be an even match...

00:13:35.000 --> 00:13:36.370
It's unfair, in fact.

00:13:36.180 --> 00:13:37.670
<b>Psst... Psst...</b>

00:13:38.900 --> 00:13:39.770
And—

00:13:39.770 --> 00:13:41.640
Enough! What's with you?!

00:13:41.640 --> 00:13:44.120
Even if there are a few problems—

00:13:44.120 --> 00:13:45.620
Don't, Yamazaki.

00:13:45.620 --> 00:13:46.800
Tonegawa-sensei...

00:13:47.910 --> 00:13:52.850
Saemon's objections are legitimate. 
He has a point.

00:13:53.730 --> 00:13:54.600
But...

00:13:55.080 --> 00:13:58.170
If you're willing to pick apart 
someone else's proposal,

00:13:58.170 --> 00:14:01.030
then you should, naturally, 
have one yourself...

00:13:58.730 --> 00:14:02.230
<b>Psst... Psst...</b>

00:14:02.610 --> 00:14:03.570
Some bright idea.

00:14:03.570 --> 00:14:04.860
<i>Psst.. Psst...</i>

00:14:05.350 --> 00:14:09.440
One that doesn't have the 
flaws you've mentioned—

00:14:09.440 --> 00:14:10.480
I do.

00:14:10.480 --> 00:14:11.390
<i>Psst...</i>

00:14:11.390 --> 00:14:14.120
I did manage to come up with one, sir!

00:14:15.860 --> 00:14:16.750
Hey, Ton!

00:14:16.750 --> 00:14:17.870
Sir?

00:14:17.870 --> 00:14:21.360
Set him up with another whiteboard.

00:14:21.360 --> 00:14:23.000
Oh, that's okay.

00:14:31.930 --> 00:14:34.180
I'm going to turn the lights off.

00:14:43.150 --> 00:14:45.650
Saemon-saburou Jirou Presents
<b>Revolutionary Rock-Paper-Scissors
Game</b>

00:14:45.650 --> 00:14:49.150
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:14:47.570 --> 00:14:51.280
Now then, if I may be so bold...

00:14:51.280 --> 00:14:56.160
I'd like to present my revolutionary 
new take on rock-paper-scissors.

00:14:56.560 --> 00:14:58.270
<i>Rock-paper-scissors?</i>

00:14:58.270 --> 00:15:01.540
<i>That was the first idea 
that got erased last time!</i>

00:15:02.130 --> 00:15:03.290
First...

00:15:03.630 --> 00:15:05.050
<b>What is a new idea?</b>

00:15:06.300 --> 00:15:10.410
How exactly are new ideas created?

00:15:10.410 --> 00:15:11.050
Well...

00:15:11.050 --> 00:15:14.300
<b>What is a new idea?</b>

00:15:11.590 --> 00:15:14.300
<b>A pre-existing idea</b>

00:15:12.430 --> 00:15:14.300
<b>And another pre-existing idea</b>

00:15:12.950 --> 00:15:14.300
<b>Combined</b>

00:15:16.050 --> 00:15:21.060
It's said that they're created by 
combining two pre-existing ideas.

00:15:21.060 --> 00:15:26.010
So, with that in mind, I took the 
pre-existing idea of rock-paper-scissors

00:15:26.010 --> 00:15:29.030
and pondered what idea to combine it with.

00:15:26.320 --> 00:15:28.780
<b>What is a new idea?</b>

00:15:26.320 --> 00:15:28.780
<b>A pre-existing idea</b>

00:15:26.320 --> 00:15:28.780
<b>And another pre-existing idea</b>

00:15:26.320 --> 00:15:28.780
<b>Combined</b>

00:15:28.880 --> 00:15:33.320
<b>Rock-Paper-Scissors</b>

00:15:29.030 --> 00:15:30.200
I chose...

00:15:30.150 --> 00:15:33.320
<b>Card Games</b>

00:15:34.520 --> 00:15:35.830
card games!

00:15:36.820 --> 00:15:39.240
C-Could this be...

00:15:39.990 --> 00:15:42.080
No, I'm sure of it.

00:15:42.080 --> 00:15:43.270
It's PP!

00:15:42.350 --> 00:15:45.230
<b>PP</b>

00:15:43.270 --> 00:15:46.590
<i>Saemon unleashes his Power Point!</i>

00:15:47.030 --> 00:15:48.550
<i>This little rat...</i>

00:15:48.550 --> 00:15:52.360
<i>He was only picking at my ideas because 
he wanted to do this, wasn't he?</i>

00:15:52.360 --> 00:15:56.090
<i>He just wanted to put on his little show!</i>

00:15:58.170 --> 00:15:59.450
<i>Idiotic!</i>

00:15:59.450 --> 00:16:02.980
<i>No matter how slick he makes it look, 
if there's no substance, it's useless!</i>

00:16:03.430 --> 00:16:06.980
<i>Nothing but a paper tiger! 
A pie in the sky!</i>

00:16:07.350 --> 00:16:11.460
<i>It's not just Tonegawa. The other 
men in black all feel the same way.</i>

00:16:11.460 --> 00:16:15.110
<i>Faced with their youngest member 
Saemon-saburou's card rock-paper-scissors,</i>

00:16:15.110 --> 00:16:18.290
<i>not a single one has any expectations!</i>

00:16:18.290 --> 00:16:20.250
<i>And yet...</i>

00:16:22.090 --> 00:16:23.510
Players receive 12 cards.

00:16:23.990 --> 00:16:27.420
Four of each: rock, paper, and scissors.

00:16:27.420 --> 00:16:30.900
In other words, 
you're limited in your choices,

00:16:30.900 --> 00:16:32.410
which is where tactics come in.

00:16:32.410 --> 00:16:33.170
<i>Psst...</i>

00:16:33.510 --> 00:16:34.540
Psst...

00:16:34.540 --> 00:16:38.180
<i>As the presentation proceeds, 
something becomes increasingly clear...</i>

00:16:35.250 --> 00:16:38.180
<b>Psst... Psst...</b>

00:16:38.180 --> 00:16:40.600
<i>His idea is completely rock-solid!</i>

00:16:40.490 --> 00:16:42.430
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:16:43.050 --> 00:16:47.190
<i>By playing rock-paper-scissors with cards, 
you limit your available choices.</i>

00:16:47.620 --> 00:16:50.920
<i>Normal rock-paper-scissors is, 
by its nature, a simple, fair game.</i>

00:16:50.920 --> 00:16:54.200
<i>Which might make you think this, 
too, is a game of luck...</i>

00:16:54.200 --> 00:16:57.390
<i>No! This is incredibly strategic!</i>

00:16:57.390 --> 00:16:59.860
<i>It has metamorphosed into a game requiring</i>

00:16:59.860 --> 00:17:03.000
<i>ingenuity, with countless 
different approaches!</i>

00:17:03.780 --> 00:17:07.690
<i>Rock-paper-scissors isn't like mahjong. 
Everyone knows the rules to it!</i>

00:17:08.250 --> 00:17:12.510
We would only need a few dozen 
competitors for it to work.

00:17:13.400 --> 00:17:14.130
It's...

00:17:14.620 --> 00:17:18.640
realistic, as well as demonic.

00:17:18.640 --> 00:17:21.890
In other words, I'm sure our target 
audience, President Hyoudou...

00:17:23.830 --> 00:17:25.390
will be fully satisfied!

00:17:23.930 --> 00:17:25.390
<b>Total Satisfaction</b>

00:17:25.390 --> 00:17:27.150
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:17:27.150 --> 00:17:29.020
<i>I-It's... perfect.</i>

00:17:30.210 --> 00:17:31.640
<i>I didn't have any expectations...</i>

00:17:32.130 --> 00:17:35.030
<i>I thought his presentation was 
going to be boring, but...</i>

00:17:35.540 --> 00:17:38.240
<i>With each bit of this explanation, 
like a newly drawn tile,</i>

00:17:38.240 --> 00:17:41.030
<i>his hand has transformed 
further and further...</i>

00:17:41.770 --> 00:17:42.950
<i>From a trash hand...</i>

00:17:43.940 --> 00:17:45.430
<i>into this!</i>

00:17:46.550 --> 00:17:49.500
<i>Tenpai... junchan, sanshoku, iipeikou!</i>

00:17:49.500 --> 00:17:51.070
<i>Psst, psst... Psst, psst...</i>

00:17:51.070 --> 00:17:53.880
<i>Tonegawa-sensei must've 
figured himself a red dora,</i>

00:17:53.880 --> 00:17:56.240
<i>with no chance he'd be discarded.</i>

00:17:56.240 --> 00:17:59.400
<i>But with the way things are 
now... he's in the way!</i>

00:17:59.900 --> 00:18:01.370
<i>There's no choice but to discard him!</i>

00:18:01.370 --> 00:18:01.940
<i>Hey.</i>

00:18:02.680 --> 00:18:08.160
<b>Psst... Psst...</b>

00:18:04.930 --> 00:18:07.480
<i>I'm pretty certain that 
every man in black here...</i>

00:18:07.480 --> 00:18:10.840
<i>No, even Ton-san!</i>

00:18:10.840 --> 00:18:13.440
<i>We've all just about agreed 
on Saemon's proposal.</i>

00:18:14.130 --> 00:18:17.950
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:18:15.830 --> 00:18:19.200
And... yeah, that does it.

00:18:20.170 --> 00:18:22.220
This concludes my presentation.

00:18:22.220 --> 00:18:23.700
Thank you for listening.

00:18:29.030 --> 00:18:30.310
<i>Psst...</i>

00:18:30.310 --> 00:18:33.050
<i>But... might makes right!</i>

00:18:30.820 --> 00:18:38.860
<i>Psst...</i>

00:18:33.050 --> 00:18:36.380
<i>Tonegawa-sensei could still 
forcibly reject this idea</i>

00:18:36.380 --> 00:18:38.860
<i>and push his own through!</i>

00:18:38.860 --> 00:18:41.010
<i>Psst... Psst... Psst...</i>

00:18:41.770 --> 00:18:43.390
<i>Psst... Psst... Psst...</i>

00:18:43.390 --> 00:18:48.020
<i>A boss, abandoning his own suggestion for 
one from the youngest member of the team?</i>

00:18:48.710 --> 00:18:50.560
<i>Not just anyone could do it.</i>

00:18:53.460 --> 00:18:57.250
<i>Will Tonegawa repeat the same mistake?!</i>

00:18:53.630 --> 00:18:57.250
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:18:57.250 --> 00:19:00.000
<i>At this rate, it'll be time for another...</i>

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:02.370
<i>employee vacation!</i>

00:19:04.490 --> 00:19:09.000
Society is truly a fascinating thing.

00:19:10.150 --> 00:19:11.620
Saemon-saburou.

00:19:11.620 --> 00:19:13.210
Y-Yes, sir?

00:19:13.210 --> 00:19:15.570
Make copies. Enough for the entire team.

00:19:17.370 --> 00:19:19.630
I want an outline for this 
card rock-paper-scissors game.

00:19:20.450 --> 00:19:22.740
It's interesting! Overwhelmingly so!

00:19:22.740 --> 00:19:23.830
We'll go with that.

00:19:23.830 --> 00:19:26.260
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:19:25.130 --> 00:19:26.260
Thank you, sir!

00:19:26.660 --> 00:19:28.790
<i>T-Tonegawa-sensei?!</i>

00:19:28.790 --> 00:19:30.770
<i>He abandoned his own idea!</i>

00:19:31.640 --> 00:19:35.520
<i>For the sake of the junchan sanshoku 
iipeikou that was card rock-paper-scissors!</i>

00:19:36.170 --> 00:19:36.940
<i>He made...</i>

00:19:38.330 --> 00:19:40.360
<i>the adult decision!</i>

00:19:40.360 --> 00:19:43.000
<i>He casts himself aside! With maturity!</i>

00:19:43.000 --> 00:19:44.780
<i>Exactly as an adult should!</i>

00:19:44.780 --> 00:19:46.830
<i>The ideal model of a boss!</i>

00:19:46.830 --> 00:19:51.790
<i>He's become an oasis amid the 
competitive hell that is a corporation!</i>

00:19:52.230 --> 00:19:55.460
Thank you! Thank you so much, sir!

00:19:56.770 --> 00:19:57.900
But...

00:19:57.900 --> 00:19:58.550
<b>Psst... Psst...</b>

00:19:59.040 --> 00:20:00.570
There's one thing.

00:20:01.510 --> 00:20:06.370
"Card Rock-Paper-Scissors" makes 
it sound like some kid's game.

00:20:06.370 --> 00:20:08.060
<b>Psst... Psst...</b>

00:20:08.710 --> 00:20:10.810
Doesn't quite put the right spin on it.

00:20:10.810 --> 00:20:12.840
R-Right.

00:20:13.370 --> 00:20:14.460
Let's see...

00:20:14.460 --> 00:20:16.310
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:20:17.640 --> 00:20:19.070
Restricted...

00:20:19.960 --> 00:20:22.570
We'll call it Restricted Rock-Paper-Scissors!

00:20:24.600 --> 00:20:25.070
<i>Psst...</i>

00:20:25.070 --> 00:20:27.130
<i>T-Tonegawa-sensei...</i>

00:20:27.130 --> 00:20:28.340
<i>Psst...</i>

00:20:27.460 --> 00:20:29.330
<i>He still forced his way in!</i>

00:20:29.750 --> 00:20:31.050
<i>But only for the title!</i>

00:20:32.460 --> 00:20:36.010
<i>Restricted Rock-Paper-Scissors is born!</i>

00:20:32.460 --> 00:20:39.020
<b>The Birth of Restricted Rock-Paper-Scissors!</b>

00:20:43.460 --> 00:20:46.990
So, why don't we play mahjong 
to decide what we do next month?

00:20:46.990 --> 00:20:49.100
I don't know how to play mahjong.

00:20:49.100 --> 00:20:51.270
Aw, you're no fun...

00:20:51.270 --> 00:20:53.390
Okay, how about rock-paper-scissors?

00:20:53.390 --> 00:20:54.890
I like the sound of that.

00:20:56.390 --> 00:20:58.450
<i>Tonegawa Yukio.</i>

00:20:59.060 --> 00:21:01.960
<i>The number two man of the Teiai Group.</i>

00:21:02.370 --> 00:21:08.760
<i>This is the story of a lone man who 
struggles between his employer,</i>

00:21:08.760 --> 00:21:13.210
<i>the president, and his own 
employees, the men in black...</i>

00:21:13.850 --> 00:21:18.850
<i>Tonegawa Yukio: Middle Manager!</i>

00:22:54.120 --> 00:22:56.550
Next time: Soul-Searching!

00:22:55.280 --> 00:23:00.250
<b>Soul-Searching</b>
